From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: replace __if_exists with a detection trait

CopyViewDimensions copies whichever dimension fields the destination view
descriptor declares, across a family of descriptors with different shapes.
MSVC expresses that with __if_exists(TDest::Field), a compile-time
member-existence test GCC cannot parse at all and which has no preprocessor
equivalent.

The standard spelling is a detection trait plus `if constexpr`, both C++17.
compat/relay_member_detect.hpp supplies RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR; view.cpp
declares one detector per field name and tests it where __if_exists stood.
Inside a template `if constexpr` discards the branch without instantiating it,
which is what makes naming a member the type does not have legal -- exactly
the property __if_exists provided.

MSVC supports both constructs, so this is one code path for every compiler
rather than an #ifdef whose GCC arm nobody exercises on Windows and whose MSVC
arm nobody exercises here.

The detector tests only the type it is asked about, matching
__if_exists(TDest::Field). Where a destination field exists and the source
lacks it this fails to compile, as the original did; that is a real mismatch
rather than something to paper over.

Why this carries a test. The failure mode is silent: a detector answering
false for a field the destination does have would simply not copy it, with no
diagnostic and a descriptor reaching the driver with a zero where a mip slice
or array size belonged. A build cannot tell a correctly discarded branch from
a wrongly discarded one, so tests/relay_member_detect_test.cpp mirrors the
function's shape -- including FirstWSlice, the one field whose destination and
source names differ -- and asserts per destination which fields arrive and
which are left alone.
---
diff --git a/include/pch.hpp b/include/pch.hpp
index bf9c37a..ad266cf 100644
--- a/include/pch.hpp
+++ b/include/pch.hpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "SharedResourceHelpers.hpp"
 #include "relay_tracelogging.hpp"
 #include "relay_msvc_pragma.hpp"
+#include "relay_member_detect.hpp"
 
 #ifndef __in
 #define __in _In_
diff --git a/src/view.cpp b/src/view.cpp
index 44bb798..913c615 100644
--- a/src/view.cpp
+++ b/src/view.cpp
@@ -221,10 +221,28 @@ RELAY_SUPPRESS_CONSTANT_CONDITIONAL // conditional expression is constant
         DeviceBase::CsSetUnorderedAccessViews(hDevice, Start, NumViews, UAVs, pInitialCounts);
     }
 
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(FirstElement)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(NumElements)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(ArraySize)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(FirstArraySlice)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(MipLevels)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(MostDetailedMip)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(PlaneSlice)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(First2DArrayFace)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(NumCubes)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(WSize)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(MipSlice)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(FirstWSlice)
+    RELAY_DEFINE_MEMBER_DETECTOR(ResourceMinLODClamp)
+
     template <typename TDest, typename TSource>
     void CopyViewDimensions(TDest& Dest, TSource const& Source)
     {
-#define COPY_FIELD(Field) __if_exists(TDest::Field) { Dest.Field = Source.Field; }
+#define COPY_FIELD(Field)                                   \
+    if constexpr (relay_has_##Field<TDest>::value)          \
+    {                                                       \
+        Dest.Field = Source.Field;                          \
+    }
         COPY_FIELD(FirstElement);
         COPY_FIELD(NumElements);
         COPY_FIELD(ArraySize);
@@ -236,11 +254,11 @@ RELAY_SUPPRESS_CONSTANT_CONDITIONAL // conditional expression is constant
         COPY_FIELD(NumCubes);
         COPY_FIELD(WSize);
         COPY_FIELD(MipSlice);
-        __if_exists(TDest::FirstWSlice)
+        if constexpr (relay_has_FirstWSlice<TDest>::value)
         {
             Dest.FirstWSlice = Source.FirstW;
         }
-        __if_exists(TDest::ResourceMinLODClamp)
+        if constexpr (relay_has_ResourceMinLODClamp<TDest>::value)
         {
             Dest.ResourceMinLODClamp = 0.0f;
         }
